requirement CHILD
title Derived child behavior
allocation value Subsystem
statement prose The subsystem shall provide the behavior allocated by the parent requirement.
rationale prose The child identifies a separately reviewable implementation responsibility.
source absent
decomposes TOP
end requirement

requirement LEAF
title Leaf timing behavior
allocation absent
statement prose The component shall complete the behavior within the interval defined by:
statement math latex t_{complete} - t_{start} \\le 100\\,\\mathrm{ms}
statement prose The interval uses a monotonic time source.
rationale null
source value TEST-SOURCE, revision A, section 4.2
decomposes CHILD
decomposes TOP
end requirement

requirement TOP
title Top-level behavior
allocation value System
statement prose The system shall provide the required externally observable behavior.
statement prose The behavior shall remain available throughout normal operation.
rationale prose The top-level requirement defines the user-visible outcome independently of implementation.
source value TEST-SOURCE, revision A, section 4
end requirement
